$plugin->release   = '1.5.39'; // SELF-REVIEW-FIX (v1.5.39 / 9 Sep 2026): Four defects found reviewing v1.5.38 before it was installed. (1) find_existing_mailbox() read the cPanel account list from $result['data'], but list_accounts() returns it under 'accounts' — the entire link-before-create fix was dead code and would never have matched anything. Now verified against both cPanel response shapes (localpart in 'login' with a separate domain, and the v136+ full address in 'login'). (2) The server mailbox list is now fetched once per request instead of once per student, so create_missing() over hundreds of students no longer makes hundreds of cPanel API calls. (3) link_account() now refuses a mailbox already linked to another student with a readable message; the unique index on email would otherwise have thrown a raw database error, and the manual type-an-address path had no such guard. (4) Cancelling the relink confirmation left the dropdown stuck on that value, so choosing the same mailbox again did nothing; the choice is now cleared. Also states in the unlink confirmation that the student's mailbox page shows no account until they are linked again. New string: error_mailboxclaimed. No DB changes. // RELINK-AND-SPLIT-FIX (v1.5.38 / 9 Sep 2026): A student could end up with two mailboxes — the address in their Moodle profile, which is where Moodle sends their mail, and a second address the plugin created and signs in to — with no way to repair it from the dashboard. Linked rows now have Relink and Unlink. Relink opens a chooser listing every mailbox available for that student, marking the one matching their Moodle profile and the one linked now, so the administrator decides which to keep; mailboxes linked to other students are never offered. Unlink removes the plugin record only — no mailbox and no message is deleted, so it is always reversible. Root cause fixed: create_email() now looks for an existing mailbox for the student (exact match on profile local part when it is on the college domain, username, ID number, configured format, firstname.lastname) and links it instead of minting a second address; controlled by the new setting prefer_existing_mailbox, on by default, and never matching a mailbox claimed by another student. Made visible: the dashboard student column now shows the Moodle profile address and warns when it differs from the linked mailbox, and the Data Quality report has a fifth check listing every student split across two mailboxes. New AJAX action: unlink_account; list_cpanel_accounts takes an optional userid and returns labelled options. New strings: success_linked_existing, success_unlinked, error_notlinked, prefer_existing_mailbox. No DB changes. // PIPELINE-COMPLIANCE (v1.5.37 / 4 Sep 2026): Clears the release pipeline blocker and four of the five warnings. The raw parameter type is gone: message bodies now use PARAM_CLEANHTML (the narrowest type that preserves rich text, and it runs clean_text() itself) and the signature uses PARAM_TEXT. mailbox.php and webmail.php now require the local/studentemail:viewown capability after require_login(). Coding style: split multi-statement lines in imap_client.php and dashboard.php; reformatted multi-line calls in ajax.php, email_manager.php, imap_client.php, mailbox.php and mailbox_ajax.php so the first argument starts on its own line; capitalised comment blocks in ajax.php, cpanel_api.php, email_manager.php and imap_client.php. The remaining ALL-CAPS warning (IMAP labels) is a checker allowlist gap and is documented, not worked around. No functional change to sending, drafts or filing. // DRAFTS-AND-SENT-FIX (v1.5.36 / 4 Sep 2026): Fixes the folder-name defect that stopped v1.5.35 filing anything. imap_list() returns the full mailbox specification including connection flags (e.g. {mail.host:993/imap/ssl}INBOX.Sent), but list_folders() stripped only the host:port form, so folder names kept the specification prefix and every later IMAP command re-specified them, producing an unaddressable mailbox. list_folders() now strips any {...} prefix, and build_mailbox_spec() refuses to specify an already-specified name. Sent/Drafts resolution now (1) matches conventional names exactly, (2) falls back to a leaf-name match, (3) probes conventional names directly with imap_status() when the folder list is unusable, (4) creates the folder only as a last resort — and every candidate is verified addressable before use. Failures are no longer silent: the Sent copy is filed before the response is sent (all IMAP waits bounded by imap_timeout) and the JSON reports sent_filed, sent_folder and a full append_log printed to the browser console by semDebug; draft saves return the same log; a failed silent draft save now raises the recovery bar instead of hiding the error with the compose pane. Added lang strings messagesent, sent_notfiled, sent_filedto, error_lock. No DB changes. // DRAFTS-AND-SENT (v1.5.35 / 2 Sep 2026): Two data-loss fixes in the student mailbox. (1) SENT COPY: every message sent over SMTP is now appended to the mailbox's real IMAP Sent folder (auto-detected: Sent / INBOX.Sent / Sent Items, created if missing), so students have a record of what they sent in Moodle, in cPanel/Roundcube webmail and in any mail client. The append runs AFTER the JSON response is flushed (fastcgi_finish_request), so a slow or unavailable Sent folder can never make a successful send look like a failure — the old blocking append that caused this is gone for good. (2) DRAFTS: closing the compose pane (backdrop click, X, Cancel, folder switch) no longer destroys the message. Compose content is kept in the pane, backed up in browser localStorage, autosaved to the IMAP Drafts folder every 25 s, saved on close, and saved on demand with a new "Save draft" button. Drafts appear in the Drafts folder everywhere; clicking one reopens it in the editor and re-saving replaces the old copy (matched on the X-SEM-Draft-Id header) instead of piling up duplicates. Sending deletes the draft it came from. A recovery bar offers any draft left behind by a browser crash or accidental tab close, and beforeunload warns about unsaved content. "Cancel" is now "Discard" and asks for confirmation. New AJAX actions: save_draft, delete_draft. New imap_client methods: append_sent_copy(), save_draft(), delete_drafts_by_id(), find_special_folder(). No DB changes. // IMAP-DEEP-DIAGNOSTIC (v1.5.33 / 29 Jul 2026): Replaced the blind "Test IMAP" button with a deep diagnostic that tries BOTH username formats (strip_domain ON and OFF) and lists every folder with its message count. New per-student "Test Mailbox" button on every active row. The diagnostic shows exactly which format connects, which has messages, and gives a one-line fix recommendation (e.g. "Toggle strip_domain OFF — opposite format has 47 messages in INBOX"). New AJAX action: test_imap_student (takes userid param). Modal result panel shows: IMAP spec used, username sent, INBOX count, all folders + counts, and a colour-coded recommendation. Savepoint 2026072900221. // IMPORT-COLLISION-FIX: import_existing() now pre-builds an in-memory map of already-linked emails from SQL before the loop — skips any match that would violate the email_idx UNIQUE constraint instead of crashing. Wrapped save_account_record() in try/catch(\dml_exception) so a single DB error never aborts the whole import. Return value now includes skipped count + error list. DIAGNOSE-SQL: diagnose_import report now includes SQL queries showing (a) emails linked to 2+ users, (b) unlinked users with identical names (collision risk), (c) status breakdown of linked accounts. // CPANEL-LOCALPART-FIX: import_existing() cpanel_map now correctly extracts localpart from login/user/email fields regardless of whether cPanel returns login as bare localpart (older) or full email (v136+). DIAGNOSE-IMPORT: New diagnostic button opens a report showing raw cPanel API response, field names, old vs fixed localpart parsing, and Moodle candidate list — so the exact mismatch can be confirmed. // DATA-QUALITY: Data Quality Report modal in dashboard header — shows duplicate Moodle accounts (same name), multiple SEM records per user, orphaned records (user deleted), and suspended-Moodle/active-cPanel mismatches. AJAX action get_data_quality added. // IMPORT-MATCH-FIX: import_existing() now correctly extracts the localpart from email-style Moodle usernames (aiop2411022@aiopms.com.au → aiop2411022) before matching against cPanel accounts — previously the @ was stripped and the candidate became nonsense, causing every match to fail silently. // FILTER-DROPDOWN: Status filter dropdown added to dashboard search bar — filter by All / Not Linked / Active / Suspended / Archived / Error. Syncs bidirectionally with the stat card click-filters. // CLEAR-EXT-BADGE: reset_password() now clears the stale "Pwd externally managed" notes badge on success — whether triggered manually (Reset PW / Fix Missing Passwords) or auto-triggered by the mailbox client on first open. // AUTO-PW-ON-IMPORT: import_existing() and link_account() now auto-generate a new cPanel password, store it encrypted, and send welcome credentials immediately — no more "Pwd externally managed" limbo requiring a manual Reset PW step. // DEBUG-CONSOLE: Full F12 DevTools debugging — semDebug() styled JS logger on every AJAX send/receive; SMTP conversation (PHPMailer SMTPDebug=3) returned in JSON smtp_log field and printed to console; X-SEM-Step response headers show last PHP checkpoint reached; X-FATAL header surfaces PHP fatals in Network tab even when body is empty. // ONE-CLICK-LINK: Link Existing now fetches unlinked cPanel accounts into a dropdown — selecting one links instantly, no typing needed. Falls back to manual text entry if cPanel is unreachable or all accounts already linked. New AJAX action: list_cpanel_accounts. Savepoint 2026062700006. // // TEST-SMTP: Added 'Test SMTP' button to admin dashboard toolbar. Calls new test_smtp AJAX action which opens a real PHPMailer smtpConnect() to the configured host/port, authenticates with one active student account's credentials, and reports success or a detailed error message — no email is sent. Savepoint 2026062700005. // FIX-MAILBOX-GETCREDS: mailbox.php called get_credentials() which does not exist — renamed to get_account_for_user(). Savepoint 2026062700004. // MAILBOX-CLIENT: Native IMAP/SMTP email client built directly into Moodle. Students click "My Email" and get a full inbox — read, compose, reply, forward, delete, folder sidebar, unread badge, search. No iframe, no Roundcube redirect. Requires PHP imap extension + SMTP settings. New settings: mailbox_enabled, smtp_host, smtp_port, smtp_encryption. lib.php updated to route "My Email" nav link to mailbox.php when enabled. Savepoint 2026062700001. // BTN-HOVER-FIX: Fixed all button hover states — added colour:#fff on :hover for every white-text button (.btn-bulk, .btn-bulk-import, all .sem-btn variants); added text-decoration:none on <a>-based button hovers. Moodle/ITALC a:hover was overriding text to red. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026062600011. // DOUBLE-NAV-FIX: Wrapped dashboard external page and settings page under a shared admin_category so only one 'Student Email Manager' entry appears in Local Plugins (previously both the external page and settings page showed as separate identically-named entries). Dashboard lang string renamed from 'Student Email Manager' to 'Dashboard'. v1.2.2: ADMINLIB-FIX: require_once adminlib.php before admin_externalpage_setup() so dashboard.php no longer crashes with "Call to undefined function". v1.2.1: BUG FIX: (1) claim_next_number() now acquires a Moodle lock (core\lock\lock_config) before reading+incrementing the counter — previously two simultaneous enrolments could both read the same counter value and be assigned identical email addresses, causing a cPanel duplicate-account error. (2) encrypt_password() now uses a random 16-byte IV per encryption stored as v2:base64(iv+ciphertext), replacing the old static IV that produced identical ciphertext for identical passwords. Decrypt supports both v2 and legacy v1 format for backwards compatibility. v1.0.0 — Initial release. Auto-provisions cPanel mailboxes for Moodle students. UAPI first, JSON API v2 fallback. AES-256-CBC encrypted passwords, four email formats, admin dashboard, auto-rules on enrolment/suspension/deletion/reactivation, student My Email portal with Roundcube link.
